  "updateView": "View",
  "updateSkip": "Skip this version",
  "updateOpenFailed": "Couldn't open the browser",
  "privacyUpdatesTitle": "Update check (off by default)",
  "privacyUpdatesBody": "When on, Troona asks GitHub once a day for the number of its latest version. \"Check for updates now\" asks once, only when you tap it. GitHub sees your IP address, as with any web request; no data about you or your music is sent. Troona never downloads or installs an update itself: \"View\" opens the release page in your browser.",
  "whatsNew110BackupTitle": "Backup and restore",
  "whatsNew110BackupBody": "Save your playlists, likes, listening history and settings to a file, and bring them back on this phone or a new one. In Settings, under Backup.",
  "whatsNew110UpdatesTitle": "Know when Troona updates",
  "whatsNew110UpdatesBody": "Turn on Check for updates in Settings: a card on Home tells you when a new version is out. Off by default, nothing is installed for you.",
  "whatsNew110ControlsTitle": "Like and resume from the lock screen",
  "whatsNew110ControlsBody": "A heart in the media notification likes the current song (Android 13 and later). After Troona is closed, the media controls resume your last song (Android 11 and later).",
  "whatsNew110RenameTitle": "Rename a playlist",
  "whatsNew110RenameBody": "Long press a playlist, then Edit playlist.",
  "whatsNew110ScreensTitle": "Small screens and large fonts",
  "whatsNew110ScreensBody": "Now Playing keeps its controls on screen on smaller phones, and the whole app follows your phone's font size.",
  "whatsNew110NotificationTitle": "Notification icon",
  "whatsNew110NotificationBody": "The playback notification shows the Troona note in the status bar.",
  "whatsNew111ChangelogTitle": "Every release in one place",
  "whatsNew111ChangelogBody": "What's new now keeps the notes of every version, the newest first. Open it any time from Settings, under Help and feedback.",
  "whatsNew111StartupTitle": "Reliable start",
  "whatsNew111StartupBody": "Troona no longer stays on its launch screen when you open it after resuming music from the media controls or a headset.",
  "whatsNew111HomeTitle": "Home right after the first scan",
  "whatsNew111HomeBody": "Your music shows on Home as soon as the first scan finds it, without refreshing.",
  "whatsNew120ArtistsTitle": "Artists from file names",
  "whatsNew120ArtistsBody": "Songs downloaded without an artist take it from their file name, such as \"Artist - Title\", and sit with that artist's other songs. The rest read Unknown artist, in your language.",
  "whatsNew120UndoTitle": "Undo a replaced queue",
  "whatsNew120UndoBody": "Starting another album while songs you added with Play next or Add to queue are still to come now offers Undo, which brings your queue back where it was.",
  "whatsNew120MenusTitle": "Menus and dialogs",
  "whatsNew120MenusBody": "Song, album and playlist menus open as a sheet in Troona's style, and dialogs fade in smoothly.",
  "whatsNew120LookTitle": "One look across the app",
  "whatsNew120LookBody": "Icons, buttons, back buttons and missing covers look the same on every screen, and buttons are easier to tap.",
  "whatsNew120PagesTitle": "Pages that slide in",
  "whatsNew120PagesBody": "Settings, the privacy policy and Your week in music no longer show the previous page through them while they open.",
  "whatsNew130ArtistsTitle": "Every artist of a song",
  "whatsNew130ArtistsBody": "A song by several artists, such as \"Nicki Minaj, Beyoncé\" or \"Chiké feat Mohbad\", now counts for each of them: it shows on every artist's page and search finds each one. Names such as \"Tyler, The Creator\" stay one artist.",
  "whatsNew130ArtistPageTitle": "Artist pages",
  "whatsNew130ArtistPageBody": "An artist's page starts with their five most played songs, then their albums, their singles, the albums they appear on and similar artists from your library.",
  "whatsNew130AlbumPageTitle": "Album pages",
  "whatsNew130AlbumPageBody": "Albums show their year, and downloaded songs without track numbers come in the order they were downloaded. Guests a title does not name show under it.",
  "whatsNew130AboutTitle": "About, when there is something to read",
  "whatsNew130AboutBody": "With online info turned on, About shows only when Last.fm has a bio or a review, with the listeners and a few genres under it.",
  "whatsNew130AlbumsTitle": "One album, not several copies",
  "whatsNew130AlbumsBody": "An album downloaded in several folders, or singles saved one folder each, showed up several times. It is one album again, and its year shows.",
  "whatsNew140TopTitle": "Back to the top",
  "whatsNew140TopBody": "Tap the tab you are on to scroll its page back to the top.",
  "whatsNew140EdgeTitle": "Edge to edge",
  "whatsNew140EdgeBody": "Lists now scroll under the status bar and the floating tab bar, on every Android version, and fade out softly under the tab bar instead of stopping on a line.",
  "whatsNew140TitlesTitle": "Large titles",
  "whatsNew140TitlesBody": "Every page opens on a large title that shrinks into a glass bar as you scroll, with the back button and the page's actions. A title left halfway settles open or closed.",
  "whatsNew140CoversTitle": "Album and playlist pages",
  "whatsNew140CoversBody": "Their cover and buttons scroll away under the same glass bar, which then shows their name.",
  "whatsNew140ArtistPhotoTitle": "Artist photos",
  "whatsNew140ArtistPhotoBody": "An artist with a photo opens on it, edge to edge, with their name over it. Pull down to enlarge it.",
  "whatsNew140SearchTitle": "Search",
  "whatsNew140SearchBody": "The search field stays pinned at the top in a glass bar while the results scroll under it, and scrolling the results closes the keyboard.",
  "whatsNew150CoverTitle": "The cover flies in",
  "whatsNew150CoverBody": "Tap an album and its cover flies from the card into place on the album page, then back when you leave.",
  "whatsNew150TitlesTitle": "Bold titles",
  "whatsNew150TitlesBody": "Large titles are bold, in the same voice as album and artist names and section titles.",
  "whatsNew150TabTitle": "A dot under the tab",
  "whatsNew150TabBody": "The tab you are on shows a dot under its icon, not only a brighter colour.",
  "whatsNew150PagesTitle": "One line of facts",
  "whatsNew150PagesBody": "Album pages state their year, song count and length, and artist pages their song count, releases and length, as one line of text instead of pills. Lossless keeps its badge.",
  "whatsNew150AlbumTitle": "Album pages",
  "whatsNew150AlbumBody": "The track list no longer has a Songs title. Under the songs, a quiet line gives the album's size and formats instead of the In your library card.",
  "whatsNew150ArtistTitle": "Artist pages",
  "whatsNew150ArtistBody": "Each song shows its album and year under its title instead of the artist's name again, and album and single cards give the year. The In your library card is gone: its counts are under the name.",
  "whatsNew150MoreByTitle": "More by",
  "whatsNew150MoreByBody": "On album pages, More by gives each album's year instead of the artist's name, with Single on singles.",
  "whatsNew150LibraryTitle": "A lighter Library",
  "whatsNew150LibraryBody": "The Library no longer shows its counts of songs, albums and artists above All.",
  "whatsNew150BackTitle": "Back where you came from",
  "whatsNew150BackBody": "Open an album's artist when you came from that artist, and you go back to their page instead of opening it again. The same goes the other way round.",
  "whatsNew150ScrollTitle": "No empty band",
  "whatsNew150ScrollBody": "An album or playlist page keeps its cover and buttons in sight while they scroll away, instead of leaving an empty band under the bar.",
  "whatsNew150NamesTitle": "Artist names with a large font",
  "whatsNew150NamesBody": "With a large font, the Library's row of artists no longer cuts their names short.",
  "whatsNew160RecapTitle": "Your listening",
  "whatsNew160RecapBody": "Any week or month at a glance: your listening time, the days you played music, your top songs, artist and albums. Open it from the card on Home, and step back with the arrows.",
  "whatsNew160StoryTitle": "Share it as a story",
  "whatsNew160StoryBody": "Turn a week or a month into an image for your stories, over your top song's colours. A finished month is shared as its Replay.",
  "whatsNew160SwipeTitle": "Swipe a song",
  "whatsNew160SwipeBody": "In the Library, albums, artists and search, swipe a song right to play it next, or left to add it to the queue.",
  "whatsNew160MiniPlayerTitle": "Swipe and hold the mini player",
  "whatsNew160MiniPlayerBody": "Swipe it left for the next song or right for the previous one. Hold it to like the song playing, or to take the like back.",
  "whatsNew160CalendarTitle": "A calendar of your listening",
  "whatsNew160CalendarBody": "Each day is a square, filled in five steps from no music to 30 plays or more. Tap a day for its count.",
  "whatsNew160MomentsTitle": "When you listen",
  "whatsNew160MomentsBody": "Your plays by weekday and time of day, with the moment that stands out, such as Friday evening. Songs played after midnight count for the night before.",
  "whatsNew160RecordTitle": "The record turns",
  "whatsNew160RecordBody": "On an album page, the record slides out of its sleeve and turns while the album plays. Tap it to play, pause or resume.",
  "whatsNew160LatestTitle": "Latest release",
  "whatsNew160LatestBody": "Artist pages show their newest album or single on its own, above the rest.",
  "whatsNew160ResumeTitle": "Pick up where you left off",
  "whatsNew160ResumeBody": "Jump back in on Home goes on from where the song stopped, with the album, artist or playlist it came from and the time left. While music plays, it opens Now Playing.",
  "whatsNew160ArtistTitle": "Artist pages",
  "whatsNew160ArtistBody": "One round Shuffle button on their photo, since an artist's songs have no order; tap a song to play in order from it. Releases come newest first, also in More by on album pages. An artist without a photo opens on a soft glow of their cover's colours.",
  "whatsNew160PlayingTitle": "The song playing looks the same everywhere",
  "whatsNew160PlayingBody": "In every list, its cover is dimmed under the moving equalizer, which stops while paused, and its title is in the accent colour.",
  "whatsNew160HapticsTitle": "One feel for haptics",
  "whatsNew160HapticsBody": "A firm tap when playback starts or stops, a light one for a skip, a refresh or a menu, and a tick for a choice. Playing a song no longer taps twice.",
  "whatsNew160BackgroundTitle": "A calmer background",
  "whatsNew160BackgroundBody": "The colours behind the tabs take two seconds to follow a new song instead of switching at once.",
  "whatsNew160BackupTitle": "Backups",
  "whatsNew160BackupBody": "They now also carry when you listen.",
  "whatsNew160HapticsOffTitle": "Vibrations with haptics off",
  "whatsNew160HapticsOffBody": "The Library's tabs at the top vibrated even with haptics turned off in Settings. They now follow the setting.",
  "whatsNew170IndexTitle": "Jump by letter",
  "whatsNew170IndexBody": "Songs, albums and artists sorted by name have an alphabetical index down the right edge.",
  "whatsNew170RecentTitle": "Recently added",
  "whatsNew170RecentBody": "The songs and albums added last, newest first, from Search and Home.",
  "whatsNew170ArtistsTitle": "Closer to the artists",
  "whatsNew170ArtistsBody": "Tap the artist's name in Now Playing to open their page. Their photo grows from the card into the page.",
  "whatsNew170AlbumMenuTitle": "Album shortcuts",
  "whatsNew170AlbumMenuBody": "Hold an album card for Play, Shuffle, Play next and Add to queue.",
  "whatsNew170NowPlayingTitle": "A smoother Now Playing",
  "whatsNew170NowPlayingBody": "Seeking lights up the ring, and closing sends the cover back into the mini player.",
  "whatsNew170ColoursTitle": "Pages in their own colours",
  "whatsNew170ColoursBody": "Album and artist pages take the colours of their cover, and open in the tab you are in.",
  "whatsNew170HomeTitle": "A lighter Home",
  "whatsNew170HomeBody": "Music comes first, with one card about the app at a time.",
  "whatsNew170QueueTitle": "Queueing with nothing playing",
  "whatsNew170QueueBody": "Play next and Add to queue now start the music when nothing plays, and an album goes into the queue whole.",
  "whatsNew170PhotosTitle": "Artist photos",
  "whatsNew170PhotosBody": "No more grey silhouettes or photos of namesakes, and Search shows the downloaded photos.",
  "whatsNew180SmartTitle": "Smart playlists",
  "whatsNew180SmartBody": "Playlists that fill themselves from rules: plays, last played, date added, likes, artist, genre, year and more. Start from a template with the + in Playlists.",
  "whatsNew180SelectionTitle": "Pick several songs",
  "whatsNew180SelectionBody": "Long press a song to start picking, then tap others. Play them, queue them or add them to a playlist in one go.",
  "whatsNew180EqualizerTitle": "Equalizer",
  "whatsNew180EqualizerBody": "On Android, from Now Playing or Settings > Playback: draw your curve with a finger or start from a preset, save it, and add up to 6 dB with Volume +.",
  "whatsNew180OrbTitle": "A button in the song's colours",
  "whatsNew180OrbBody": "The centre of the tab bar glows in the colours of the song playing. Tap it to open Now Playing, or to start music when nothing is loaded.",
  "whatsNew180GlassTitle": "Glass effects for every phone",
  "whatsNew180GlassBody": "Balanced keeps the blur in page headers only and No blur draws none, both with tinted surfaces: smoother scrolling on older phones. In Settings.",
  "whatsNew180MiniPlayerTitle": "A smoother mini player",
  "whatsNew180MiniPlayerBody": "Swipe to the next or previous song and the titles follow your finger while the cover fades. Swipe down to close it.",
  "whatsNew180ReadableTitle": "Easier to read",
  "whatsNew180ReadableBody": "Small grey text has more contrast, and Now Playing's ring reads over every cover.",
  "whatsNew180GlassFixTitle": "Glass settings apply at once",
  "whatsNew180GlassFixBody": "Changing the glass effects now redraws every screen right away, not only the ones opened afterwards.",
